    Don't index themes anymore (#6640)
    
    Fixes #5264.
    
    Removes all code that relates themes to the index. For services like the
    admin ui that require detailed query capabilities, a new function has
    been added to the themes database.
    
    See related issue for motivation.
    
    Of course, this patch cannot remove any actual indices from
    ElasticSearch/OpenSearch installations. So if you really want themes
    gone from your index you'll have to nuke and rebuild it, or send a query
    directly to your index that gets rid of them. Not doing so should not be
    a problem though.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    This mostly affects the admin ui and the listprovider, so be sure to
    check that those work as before.
    
    
